Sir Arctos is a polar bear who gained speech and reason, a knight of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]]. He was brought from [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]] and knighted by Aurelia VII, the Church's pontifex. He wears pearlescent plate over his fur, a purple cloak and a wide-brimmed hat, and carries a bastard sword and a shield. He keeps a monocle for poor sight in one eye, and calls himself a very smart bear. He eats from a bowl stamped with his name, using silver cutlery.

He was once the pet of Minister [[People/Valerius Vane|Valerius Vane]], before the [[Iridescent Host|Host]] gave him speech, and says the two are equals now. He keeps a flat at the Vane estate. He is devout: he heals by the Host's power, casts [[Phenomena/Augury|augury]], has worked toward preaching and a parish of his own, and has asked the Host why he was awakened when he could have stayed a sleeping bear. He also took the mark of [[Aut]] on his chest, by his own request; it stays hidden unless he calls it.

He joined [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] in the wake of the deaths at the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|Crowded Flea]], and travels with [[People/Johnny|Johnny]], [[People/Anzu|Anzu]], [[People/Benny|Benny]] and [[People/Argyle|Argyle]]. He has a fan club of five in [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]], all in prison for trying to break into Vane's manor to meet him.

Over the Party's six months of downtime he launched a soft drink, [[Phenomena/Polar Shiv|Polar Shiv]], made by [[Org/Ternion Heavy Industries/index|Ternion Heavy Industries]] and sold with [[Phenomena/Shiver|shiver]] in it or without. He chose to stay in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] to run it rather than go on the pilgrimage.
